[{:db/id 17592186166801 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f6fc6d8a-4eb7-5088-83d3-79243011f5cd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f6fc6d8a-4eb7-5088-83d3-79243011f5cd" :question/id #uuid "f6fc6d8a-4eb7-5088-83d3-79243011f5cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-96301" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 \\\\ -10 & 20\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: Notice that from the matrix $Σ,$ we can deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=5$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$ without solving the characteristic equation.\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=25,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-25I & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 \\\\ -10 & 20\\end{aligned}]-25[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-20 & -10 \\\\ -10 & -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-25I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-0I & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 \\\\ -10 & 20\\end{aligned}]-0[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 \\\\ -10 & 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-0I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of $A{A}^{T}$): Since the first singular value is not zero, and we know the corresponding singular right vector, we can compute the first column of $U$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, we can't use the same formula to find the second column of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find a vector\n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nsuch that \n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,‖{u}_{2}‖=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nSolving ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{1}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{2}=0,\n$$\n\nwe get a nonzero solution $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Normalizing this vector, we finally obtain the  second column of $U:$ \n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-71d21d04-b8cf-52fb-b69f-913fac3a02a0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-71d21d04-b8cf-52fb-b69f-913fac3a02a0" :answer-field/id #uuid "71d21d04-b8cf-52fb-b69f-913fac3a02a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-819539d5-8368-5aa3-94ce-d7df6851587e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e817a50e-0df8-5d71-a4b4-65cf2d407ecf" "answer-819539d5-8368-5aa3-94ce-d7df6851587e" "answer-022c280c-4887-5547-b534-3eab18d91351" "answer-ea25ef23-0653-5956-9e57-5f22e9b5fc3c" "answer-60abb16a-0ac6-577a-bfde-4a57f5e0f9e7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e817a50e-0df8-5d71-a4b4-65cf2d407ecf" :answer/id #uuid "e817a50e-0df8-5d71-a4b4-65cf2d407ecf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-819539d5-8368-5aa3-94ce-d7df6851587e" :answer/id #uuid "819539d5-8368-5aa3-94ce-d7df6851587e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$ and $V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-022c280c-4887-5547-b534-3eab18d91351" :answer/id #uuid "022c280c-4887-5547-b534-3eab18d91351" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea25ef23-0653-5956-9e57-5f22e9b5fc3c" :answer/id #uuid "ea25ef23-0653-5956-9e57-5f22e9b5fc3c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60abb16a-0ac6-577a-bfde-4a57f5e0f9e7" :answer/id #uuid "60abb16a-0ac6-577a-bfde-4a57f5e0f9e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & -\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}]$ and $V=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166799 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f1ec3544-a33f-5f0c-9945-54a8126d4c0d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f1ec3544-a33f-5f0c-9945-54a8126d4c0d" :question/id #uuid "f1ec3544-a33f-5f0c-9945-54a8126d4c0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-96425" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}40 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 40\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: Notice that since ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is diagonal, the singular values of $A$ are \n\n$\\,$ ${\\sigma }_{1}={\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{40}.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$): Seeking non-zero solutions of $({A}^{T}\\,A-40I)v=0,$ we obtain the unit eigenvectors \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{40}}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{40}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{40}}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{40}}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U,$ $Σ,$ and $V:$ \n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{40} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{40}\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-447ffdf8-023f-57e3-bed2-848fc5a564b6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-447ffdf8-023f-57e3-bed2-848fc5a564b6" :answer-field/id #uuid "447ffdf8-023f-57e3-bed2-848fc5a564b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d5e2a007-8f0c-57af-8541-d911365e32dc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fa0df3c9-5acc-5e18-a261-80436751da0e" "answer-b147b04e-81e4-5cae-9ace-85831654e31f" "answer-d011d1a3-0ba8-5816-b392-eed450cd5db0" "answer-d5e2a007-8f0c-57af-8541-d911365e32dc" "answer-820ad6ba-f7d5-5582-b70e-ebb9b1ceffe2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa0df3c9-5acc-5e18-a261-80436751da0e" :answer/id #uuid "fa0df3c9-5acc-5e18-a261-80436751da0e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$ and $V=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b147b04e-81e4-5cae-9ace-85831654e31f" :answer/id #uuid "b147b04e-81e4-5cae-9ace-85831654e31f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$ and $V=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d011d1a3-0ba8-5816-b392-eed450cd5db0" :answer/id #uuid "d011d1a3-0ba8-5816-b392-eed450cd5db0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$ and $V=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5e2a007-8f0c-57af-8541-d911365e32dc" :answer/id #uuid "d5e2a007-8f0c-57af-8541-d911365e32dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$ and $V=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-820ad6ba-f7d5-5582-b70e-ebb9b1ceffe2" :answer/id #uuid "820ad6ba-f7d5-5582-b70e-ebb9b1ceffe2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\end{aligned}]$ and $V=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-1fc3e9bb-349e-5fb5-a883-56163930d8c0" :activity/id #uuid "1fc3e9bb-349e-5fb5-a883-56163930d8c0" :activity/title "Singular Value Decomposition of 2x2 Matrices With Zero or Repeated Eigenvalues" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050770 :activity/course 17592186046660 :activity/steps ["step-ad6e7d37-c775-5b7b-b349-eb9dee4a1453" "step-d2f6c29c-1b1d-523c-bac9-0e9e225514e2" "step-eb53c4bf-fd89-5cbd-9fad-7e1f192d2578" "step-bce2f3bf-424e-54b0-b537-ee61a51b4d2b" "step-3868de93-336f-5be1-b8c0-ee5d1d36c94c"] :activity/first-step "step-ad6e7d37-c775-5b7b-b349-eb9dee4a1453" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-ad6e7d37-c775-5b7b-b349-eb9dee4a1453" :step/id #uuid "ad6e7d37-c775-5b7b-b349-eb9dee4a1453" :step/content "question-f6fc6d8a-4eb7-5088-83d3-79243011f5cd" :step/next "step-d2f6c29c-1b1d-523c-bac9-0e9e225514e2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d2f6c29c-1b1d-523c-bac9-0e9e225514e2" :step/id #uuid "d2f6c29c-1b1d-523c-bac9-0e9e225514e2" :step/content 17592186371353 :step/next "step-eb53c4bf-fd89-5cbd-9fad-7e1f192d2578" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-eb53c4bf-fd89-5cbd-9fad-7e1f192d2578" :step/id #uuid "eb53c4bf-fd89-5cbd-9fad-7e1f192d2578" :step/content 17592186404878 :step/next "step-bce2f3bf-424e-54b0-b537-ee61a51b4d2b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-bce2f3bf-424e-54b0-b537-ee61a51b4d2b" :step/id #uuid "bce2f3bf-424e-54b0-b537-ee61a51b4d2b" :step/content "question-f1ec3544-a33f-5f0c-9945-54a8126d4c0d" :step/next "step-3868de93-336f-5be1-b8c0-ee5d1d36c94c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3868de93